{
  "abstract": "On an m-dimensional space V of bounded functions on an arbitrary set Ω, and for every ε > 0, there is a finitely supported probability measure ϱ = ∑ₖ wₖ δ(xₖ) for which the uniform norm on V is dominated by the L₂(ϱ) norm with the constant √(m + ε): |f(y)|² ≤ (m + ε) ∑ₖ wₖ |f(xₖ)|² for every y ∈ Ω and every f ∈ V. For continuous functions on a compact domain the same holds with ε = 0. In both cases at most m² + 1 points are needed. The measure is one whose Gram matrix has an almost maximal determinant.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Mario Ullrich"
    }
  ],
